LOCAL1="Display power control failed"
LOCAL2="Display power control failed on %s: the program cec-ctl could not be started (%s). The TV will not go to standby or wake with the screen. Check that the package v4l-utils is installed, then switch the screen off and on to try again."
LOCAL3="Display power control failed on %s: the HDMI-CEC adapter %s has no usable address. The TV will not go to standby or wake with the screen. Check that HDMI-CEC is switched on in the TV's settings (it may be called Anynet+, Bravia Sync or Simplink) and that the cable is in the TV's HDMI-CEC input, then switch the screen off and on to try again."
LOCAL4="Display power control failed on %s: the TV did not acknowledge %s. The TV may not go to standby or wake with the screen. Check that HDMI-CEC is switched on in the TV's settings, then switch the screen off and on to try again."
LOCAL5="Display power control is off: the login session could not be found or read (%s), so no TV is told to stand by or wake. Log out and in again; if it repeats, check that systemd-logind is running."
LOCAL6="Open Display settings"
